  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "2 Chronicles",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 16,
    "summary": "Asa employs Syria to defeat Israel—Hanani the seer reproves Asa for lack of faith—Asa suffers from disease and dies.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "In the six and thirtieth year of the reign of Asa Baasha king of Israel came up against Judah, and built Ramah, to the intent that he might let none go out or come in to Asa king of Judah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 16:1",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Asa brought out silver and gold out of the treasures of the house of the Lord and of the king’s house, and sent to Ben-hadad king of Syria, that dwelt at Damascus, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 16:2",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a league between me and thee, as there was between my father and thy father: behold, I have sent thee silver and gold; go, break thy league with Baasha king of Israel, that he may depart from me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 16:3",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ben-hadad hearkened unto king Asa, and sent the captains of his armies against the cities of Israel; and they smote Ijon, and Dan, and Abel-maim, and all the store cities of Naphtali.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 16:4",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, when Baasha heard it, that he left off building of Ramah, and let his work cease.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 42
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 16:5",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Asa the king took all Judah; and they carried away the stones of Ramah, and the timber thereof, wherewith Baasha was building; and he built therewith Geba and Mizpah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 16:6",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And at that time Hanani the seer came to Asa king of Judah, and said unto him, Because thou hast relied on the king of Syria, and not relied on the Lord thy God, therefore is the host of the king of Syria escaped out of thine hand.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "TG Seer."
          },
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 115,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 15:18."
          },
          {
            "start": 134,
            "end": 140,
            "text": "D&C 30:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 199,
            "end": 204,
            "text": "Septuagint: Israel."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Seer.",
            "prettyString": "TG Seer",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
